---
layout: base.njk
title: Submit a Prompt
description: Add your prompt to the NekoGrimoire gallery.
---
<div class="prose">
  <h1 class="detail-title" style="margin-top:36px;">Submit a Prompt</h1>
  <p>
    Every entry in the grimoire lives as one JSON file in
    <code>/prompts/</code>, plus optional images in <code>/images/</code>.
    You don't need <code>git</code> or the command line — fill out the form
    below and it builds the file + a ready-to-open GitHub link for you.
    You'll need a (free) GitHub account to open the pull request.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    Prefer to do it by hand, or the auto-generated link is too long to open?
    Copy the JSON at the bottom of this form and paste it into a new file at
    <code>prompts/&lt;your-slug&gt;.json</code> using GitHub's
    <a href="https://github.com/{{ site.repo }}/new/{{ site.defaultBranch }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“create new file”</a>
    page, following the same schema as
    <a href="https://github.com/{{ site.repo }}/blob/{{ site.defaultBranch }}/prompts/example-neon-alley-cat.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">this example</a>.
  </div>
</div>

<div class="form-card">
  <div class="field">
    <label for="f-title">Title *</label>
    <input type="text" id="f-title" placeholder="Neon Alley Cat" />
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="f-credit-name">Author</label>
    <span class="hint">Whoever should get credit — you, or someone else if you're sharing their prompt.</span>
    <input type="text" id="f-credit-name" placeholder="their-handle" />
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="f-credit-url">Author's link (X/Twitter, portfolio, etc.)</label>
    <input type="url" id="f-credit-url" placeholder="https://x.com/your-handle" />
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="f-tags">Tags</label>
    <input type="text" id="f-tags" placeholder="cyberpunk, cat, portrait" />
    <span class="hint">Comma-separated.</span>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label>Step 1 (optional) — image(s)</label>
    <span class="hint">
      Upload your result image(s) to GitHub first, then list the exact filename(s) you used below, one per line.
      This opens as its own small pull request, separate from the one step 2 creates below — that's fine, a
      maintainer can merge both together.
    </span>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <button type="button" class="btn secondary" id="upload-link-btn">Open GitHub image upload →</button>
    </div>
    <textarea id="f-images" rows="2" placeholder="neon-alley-cat-1.jpg"></textarea>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <label>Step 2 — prompt version(s) *</label>
    <span class="hint">Add one entry per AI model or per variation of the prompt.</span>
    <div id="versions"></div>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <button type="button" class="btn secondary" id="add-version-btn">+ Add another version</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="btn-row">
    <button type="button" class="btn" id="generate-btn">Generate &amp; open pull request →</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn secondary" id="copy-json-btn">Copy JSON instead</button>
  </div>

  <div class="field" style="margin-top:18px;">
    <label>Preview</label>
    <textarea id="f-preview" rows="10" readonly></textarea>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  window.NEKOGRIMOIRE_CONFIG = {
    repo: {{ site.repo | jsonStringify | safe }},
    branch: {{ site.defaultBranch | jsonStringify | safe }}
  };
</script>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/submit.js' | url }}"></script>
